WEBVTT

NOTE
Authored in-project for the Changeover demo rig. This is NOT a Blender-origin
subtitle file and does not claim to be: the on-screen caption TEXT is authored
test content written for this project. What IS real is the cue TIMING -- each
cue start/end is placed on a real frame boundary of fixtures/source.mp4
(29.97 fps / 30000:1001, 179.212s, 5371 frames), so a producer diffing cue
timestamps against an advancing program clock is measuring a real quantity.

The video is Tears of Steel (c) Blender Foundation, CC BY 3.0, used as the
open-license program feed. The caption text below is ours.

Cue cadence is deliberately ~2s with ~0.5s gaps so that a stalled cue producer
is measurable against the program clock within a few seconds.

